IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`

-- g9-sched1-commissioner.l4: Schedule 1 to the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, "Jersey Charity Commissioner" (Article 3): the appointment, status, termination of office,
-- staff, resources and reporting of the Commissioner. Quotations are copied by srcrefs.py from the text of the Law (src:N is line N of that file) and every rule carries an @ref with the lines it rests on.
-- Units: a day is a calendar date, a period is counted in the days, weeks, months and years of the calendar as the fork on it says (see g9-common.l4).
-- The Minister, the Commissioner and the States are the roles `the Minister`, `the Commissioner` and `the States` of `Legal actor`; which person holds an office is a separate fact.
-- A discretion of the Minister or the Commissioner ("appearing to the Minister to be suitable", "satisfying himself or herself", "considers are required") is an INPUT.
-- The Law's two additions "subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017" (paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7)) exist only in the texts from 16 December 2019 (trap T22, fork F9.9).
-- Paragraph 4(12) of the Law says "paragraph (11)" where it means sub-paragraph (11); the cross-reference is read as sub-paragraph (11) (see the contradictions in FRAGMENT-G9.md).

§ `Schedule 1: Jersey Charity Commissioner (Article 3)`

-- The heading of Schedule 1 carries endnote [5]: "Schedule 1 amended by L.1/2017". L.1/2017 Article 30(3) added "subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017" at the beginning of
-- paragraph 2(4)(a) and "Subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the" in place of "The" at the beginning of paragraph 4(7), from 16 December 2019 (Table of Legislation History).
-- The text read here is the text of 2 October 2026, which has the words; the rules that depend on them take the vintage of the text as an input.
-- src:754 | Schedule 1[5]
-- src:755 | (Article 3)
-- src:756 | Jersey Charity Commissioner
@ref Schedule 1 (heading) and endnote [5] (src:754-756)
`Sch 1 the heading Jersey Charity Commissioner (inert)` MEANS
    "Schedule 1[5] (Article 3) Jersey Charity Commissioner"

§§ `The acts of Schedule 1`

-- Each act names who does it: the first actor of an act is its performer (an actor may only perform its own acts).
DECLARE `Act under Schedule 1` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 1: appoint a person as the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission on an appointment as the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: present to the States a notice of intention to appoint a person as the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: determine the period of an appointment as the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: re-appoint the person serving as the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: take all reasonable steps to ensure that the office of the Commissioner is filled` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: resign from the office of the Commissioner by notice in writing to the Minister` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: terminate the appointment of the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated the appointment of the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: pay to the income of the States the fees and other sums received by the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: make staff available to the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: designate a person as the relevant person to be treated as the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: provide accommodation and equipment for the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: prepare and publish a report on the activities of the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: provide the Minister with the report of the Commissioner` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: lay a copy of the report of the Commissioner before the States` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: give directions to the Commissioner on the content and form of the report, by written notice that is published` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `Sch 1: give a direction that requires the report to justify a decision about an individual charity, governor or applicant` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`

`Sch 1: the Minister appoints a person as the Commissioner` MEANS `Sch 1: appoint a person as the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister seeks the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission` MEANS `Sch 1: seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission on an appointment as the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States` MEANS `Sch 1: present to the States a notice of intention to appoint a person as the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister determines the period of the appointment` MEANS `Sch 1: determine the period of an appointment as the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister re-appoints the person serving` MEANS `Sch 1: re-appoint the person serving as the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister takes all reasonable steps to fill the office` MEANS `Sch 1: take all reasonable steps to ensure that the office of the Commissioner is filled` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Commissioner resigns by notice in writing` MEANS `Sch 1: resign from the office of the Commissioner by notice in writing to the Minister` `the Commissioner`
`Sch 1: the Minister terminates the appointment` MEANS `Sch 1: terminate the appointment of the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of the termination to the States` MEANS `Sch 1: present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated the appointment of the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Commissioner pays fees and other sums to the income of the States` MEANS `Sch 1: pay to the income of the States the fees and other sums received by the Commissioner` `the Commissioner`
`Sch 1: the Minister makes staff available` MEANS `Sch 1: make staff available to the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister designates a relevant person` MEANS `Sch 1: designate a person as the relevant person to be treated as the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister provides accommodation and equipment` MEANS `Sch 1: provide accommodation and equipment for the Commissioner` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Commissioner prepares and publishes the report` MEANS `Sch 1: prepare and publish a report on the activities of the Commissioner` `the Commissioner`
`Sch 1: the Commissioner provides the Minister with the report` MEANS `Sch 1: provide the Minister with the report of the Commissioner` `the Commissioner`
`Sch 1: the Minister lays a copy of the report before the States` MEANS `Sch 1: lay a copy of the report of the Commissioner before the States` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister gives directions on the report` MEANS `Sch 1: give directions to the Commissioner on the content and form of the report, by written notice that is published` `the Minister`
`Sch 1: the Minister directs that the report justify a decision` MEANS `Sch 1: give a direction that requires the report to justify a decision about an individual charity, governor or applicant` `the Minister`

§§ `1 Appointment of Commissioner`

-- What the Law fixes about one appointment, or re-appointment, of the Commissioner (1(6): references in paragraph 1 to appointment include re-appointment).
-- `the day the term expires` is the end date of the period determined under 1(5); fork F9.2 says what an end date denotes.
DECLARE `Appointment of the Commissioner` HAS
    `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister makes the appointment (or re-appointment)
    `the first day of the term` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person holds the office under this appointment
    `the day the term expires` IS A DATE @desc The end date of the period determined by the Minister under paragraph 1(5)
    `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's opinion under paragraph 1(1): an input, not computed
    `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day on which the Minister sought the views (paragraph 1(2)); NOTHING if never
    `a notice of intention was presented to the States on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day on which the Minister presented the notice (paragraph 1(3)); NOTHING if never
    `the person was serving as the Commissioner on the day of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE for a re-appointment of a person serving (paragraph 1(6))
    `the term is followed by a re-appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE where the person is re-appointed when this term expires, so that the expiry is not "without re-appointment" (paragraph 3(4)(a))
    `the day on which the person became a member of the States` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the person is not a member of the States (paragraph 3(4)(b))
    `the service before this appointment` IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules` @desc The periods of service as the Commissioner (or as a designated relevant person) before this appointment, earliest first (paragraph 3(4)(c))

-- src:758 | (1) The Minister must appoint a person appearing to the Minister to be suitable to hold the office of the Commissioner.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(1) (src:758)
@export The Minister's duty to appoint a person appearing to the Minister to be suitable to hold the office of the Commissioner, while the office is vacant
GIVEN `the office of the Commissioner is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE while no person is appointed as the Commissioner; the Law states no other trigger for the duty
      `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's opinion that the person is suitable to hold the office: an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 1(1) the Minister must appoint a person appearing to the Minister to be suitable` `the office of the Commissioner is vacant` `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable` MEANS
    IF `the office of the Commissioner is vacant`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 1: the Minister appoints a person as the Commissioner`
         PROVIDED `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not appoint a person appearing to the Minister to be suitable to hold the office of the Commissioner"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The parenthesis of 1(2), "without prejudice to the powers of the States or the Jersey Appointments Commission under Article 15 of that Law", preserves those powers and adds no rule here.
-- src:759 | (2) Before appointing a person as the Commissioner, the Minister must seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission, established by Article 17 of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005, on the appointment (without prejudice to the powers of the States or the Jersey Appointments Commission under Article 15 of that Law).
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(2) (src:759)
@export The Minister's duty to seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission before appointing the Commissioner, with the last day for it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the appointment (or re-appointment) is made
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 1(2) before appointing a person the Minister must seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission` interp `the day of the appointment` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 1: the Minister seeks the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission`
    BEFORE (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission to be sought` interp `the day of the appointment`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission before appointing"

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(2) (src:759)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1(2) the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before the appointment` interp appointment MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment's `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST sought THEN `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` interp sought (appointment's `the day of the appointment`)

-- src:760 | (3) The Minister must, at least 2 weeks before appointing a person as the Commissioner, present to the States a notice of his or her intention to make the appointment.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(3) (src:760)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing` MEANS 2

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(3) (src:760)
@export The Minister's duty to present to the States a notice of intention at least 2 weeks before appointing the Commissioner, with the last day for it counted as the chosen reading says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the appointment (or re-appointment) is made
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 1(3) at least 2 weeks before appointing the Minister must present to the States a notice of intention` interp `the day of the appointment` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States`
    BEFORE (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of intention before an appointment` interp `the day of the appointment` `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not present to the States a notice of intention at least 2 weeks before appointing"

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(3) (src:760)
@export Whether the notice of intention to appoint or re-appoint the Commissioner was presented to the States in time, that is at least 2 weeks before the appointment, counted as the chosen reading says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The appointment or re-appointment and the dates of its steps
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` interp appointment MEANS
    CONSIDER appointment's `a notice of intention was presented to the States on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST presented
        THEN `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` interp presented (appointment's `the day of the appointment`) `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention must be presented at least this many weeks before appointing`

-- 1(4) is inert: it says the person holds and vacates the office in accordance with the terms of the appointment, subject to the Law. The terms of the appointment are not in the Law; what the Law
-- itself says about vacating the office is in paragraph 3, and the period of the appointment is fixed by 1(5), so 1(4) adds no rule of its own.
-- src:761 | (4) A person appointed as the Commissioner holds and vacates that office in accordance with the terms of his or her appointment, subject to this Law.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(4) (src:761)
`Sch 1 para 1(4) the terms of the appointment (inert)` MEANS
    "(4) A person appointed as the Commissioner holds and vacates that office in accordance with the terms of his or her appointment, subject to this Law."

-- src:762 | (5) When appointing a person as the Commissioner the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(5) (src:762)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is not more than this many years` MEANS 6

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(5) (src:762)
@export Whether the period the Minister determined for an appointment or re-appointment of the Commissioner is within the limit of not more than 6 years, counted as the chosen reading says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The appointment or re-appointment, with its first day and the end date of its period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` interp appointment MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` interp (appointment's `the first day of the term`) (appointment's `the day the term expires`) `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is not more than this many years`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(5) (src:762)
@export The Minister's duty, when appointing the Commissioner, to determine a period of the appointment of not more than 6 years
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The appointment or re-appointment, with the dates of its steps and the facts that bear on its expiry
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 1(5) when appointing the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years` interp appointment MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 1: the Minister determines the period of the appointment`
    PROVIDED `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` interp appointment
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not determine a period of the appointment of not more than 6 years"

-- src:763 | (6) The Minister may re-appoint a person serving as the Commissioner (and references in this paragraph to appointment include re-appointment).
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(6) (src:763)
@export The Minister's power to re-appoint a person serving as the Commissioner
GIVEN `the person is serving as the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person to be re-appointed is serving as the Commissioner when the Minister re-appoints
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 1(6) the Minister may re-appoint a person serving as the Commissioner` `the person is serving as the Commissioner` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Sch 1: the Minister re-appoints the person serving`
    PROVIDED `the person is serving as the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- 1(6) also says that references in paragraph 1 to appointment include re-appointment, so the rules of 1(2), 1(3) and 1(5) above are asked of a re-appointment as of an appointment:
-- both are an `Appointment of the Commissioner`, a re-appointment being one whose field `the person was serving as the Commissioner on the day of the appointment` is TRUE.

-- src:764 | (7) The Minister must take all reasonable steps to ensure that at all times the office of the Commissioner is filled.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(7) (src:764)
@export The Minister's duty to take all reasonable steps to ensure that the office of the Commissioner is filled at all times
GIVEN `the office of the Commissioner is filled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if a person is appointed as the Commissioner on the day in question
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 1(7) the Minister must take all reasonable steps to ensure that at all times the office of the Commissioner is filled` `the office of the Commissioner is filled` MEANS
    IF `the office of the Commissioner is filled`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 1: the Minister takes all reasonable steps to fill the office`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not take all reasonable steps to ensure that the office of the Commissioner is filled"

-- The duty is to take all reasonable steps, not to succeed: an unfilled office is no breach if all reasonable steps were taken, and whether they were is an input.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(7) (src:764)
GIVEN `the office of the Commissioner is filled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if a person is appointed as the Commissioner on the day in question
      `the Minister has taken all reasonable steps to ensure that the office is filled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination (the Minister's or the court's) that all reasonable steps were taken: an input
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1(7) the Minister has complied with the duty to keep the office filled` `the office of the Commissioner is filled` `the Minister has taken all reasonable steps to ensure that the office is filled` MEANS
    `the office of the Commissioner is filled` OR `the Minister has taken all reasonable steps to ensure that the office is filled`

-- 1(8) is inert: it says that 1(7) does not stop the terms of an appointment from requiring work for only a limited number of days in a year or hours in a day.
-- It restricts how 1(7) is read (a part-time Commissioner fills the office) and creates no rule, input or outcome of its own.
-- src:765 | (8) Nothing in sub-paragraph (7) is to be construed as preventing the terms of a person’s appointment from requiring the person to work under the appointment for only a limited number of days in a year or hours in a day.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 1(8) (src:765)
`Sch 1 para 1(8) part-time terms of appointment (inert)` MEANS
    "(8) Nothing in sub-paragraph (7) is to be construed as preventing the terms of a person’s appointment from requiring the person to work under the appointment for only a limited number of days in a year or hours in a day."

§§ `2 Status of Commissioner`

-- 2(1) is inert: the five things a corporation sole may do in the name of the office are legal capacities, each without precondition or outcome that any rule of the Law turns on.
-- (The Commissioner can be charged with an offence: Article 29(1) (src:664-667) creates an offence for "a person who receives information ... under or for the purposes of this Law" and discloses it without consent, which on its words reaches the Commissioner too.)
-- src:767 | (1) The Commissioner may, as a corporation sole, in the name of his or her office –
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1) (src:767)
`Sch 1 para 2(1) the Commissioner as a corporation sole (inert)` MEANS
    "(1) The Commissioner may, as a corporation sole, in the name of his or her office –"
-- 2(1)(a): a capacity to contract for any purpose of the office. Inert: no precondition and no outcome.
-- src:768 | (a) enter into an agreement for any purpose of his or her office;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1)(a) (src:768)
`Sch 1 para 2(1)(a) enter into an agreement (inert)` MEANS
    "(a) enter into an agreement for any purpose of his or her office;"
-- 2(1)(b): a capacity to hold movable property. Inert: no precondition and no outcome.
-- src:769 | (b) acquire, hold and dispose of movable property;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1)(b) (src:769)
`Sch 1 para 2(1)(b) acquire, hold and dispose of movable property (inert)` MEANS
    "(b) acquire, hold and dispose of movable property;"
-- 2(1)(c): a capacity to sue and be sued. Inert: no precondition and no outcome.
-- src:770 | (c) sue and be sued in any civil proceedings;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1)(c) (src:770)
`Sch 1 para 2(1)(c) sue and be sued in civil proceedings (inert)` MEANS
    "(c) sue and be sued in any civil proceedings;"
-- 2(1)(d): a capacity to be charged with an offence and defend criminal proceedings. Inert: the offences themselves are in the Articles that create them, and no rule here turns on the capacity.
-- src:771 | (d) be charged with an offence and defend criminal proceedings; and
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1)(d) (src:771)
`Sch 1 para 2(1)(d) be charged with an offence and defend criminal proceedings (inert)` MEANS
    "(d) be charged with an offence and defend criminal proceedings; and"
-- 2(1)(e): a capacity to do what is reasonably necessary or expedient for the Commissioner's functions; it overlaps Article 4(2), which is encoded with Article 4. Inert here: no precondition and no outcome.
-- src:772 | (e) do anything reasonably necessary or expedient for or incidental to any of the Commissioner’s functions.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(1)(e) (src:772)
`Sch 1 para 2(1)(e) do anything reasonably necessary or expedient for the Commissioner's functions (inert)` MEANS
    "(e) do anything reasonably necessary or expedient for or incidental to any of the Commissioner’s functions."
-- 2(2) is inert: a statement of status. It limits no rule of this Law except that directions under 4(11) must respect the independence (4(12), encoded).
-- src:773 | (2) The Commissioner is independent of the States and the Minister.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(2) (src:773)
`Sch 1 para 2(2) the Commissioner is independent of the States and the Minister (inert)` MEANS
    "(2) The Commissioner is independent of the States and the Minister."
-- 2(3) is inert: a statement that the terms of appointment create no contract of employment or agency. It has no input, condition or outcome in this Law; employment law is outside the sources.
-- src:774 | (3) The terms and conditions of the appointment of the Commissioner must not be construed so as to create a contract of employment or agency between the States, or the Minister, and the person appointed.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(3) (src:774)
`Sch 1 para 2(3) the terms of appointment create no contract of employment or agency (inert)` MEANS
    "(3) The terms and conditions of the appointment of the Commissioner must not be construed so as to create a contract of employment or agency between the States, or the Minister, and the person appointed."

-- 2(4) is the chapeau of the two rules below: "Despite sub-paragraphs (2) and (3)". It overrides nothing that is computed: 2(2) and 2(3) are inert, so the chapeau is carried as the heading of the two rules.
-- src:775 | (4) Despite sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) –
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(4) (src:775)
`Sch 1 para 2(4) despite sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(4) Despite sub-paragraphs (2) and (3) –"

-- The rule shared by 2(4)(a) and 4(7): who must bear a cost in the text read. From 16 December 2019 (L.1/2017) both are "subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017",
-- which lets an Order under that Article direct distributions from the Fund towards the cost of the Commissioner's remuneration, staff, accommodation and equipment (Article 20(2)(a) of that Law).
-- The Order, and the Fund, are other enactments: whether an Order directs the cost to the Fund is an input. F9.9 reading A: the cost the Order directs to the Fund is borne by the Fund in place of the annual income of the States.
-- Reading B: the States remain liable and the Fund only reimburses them. In a text without the words (before 16 December 2019) the annual income of the States bears the cost whatever any Order says.
-- src:776 | (a) subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the remuneration or other payment for services of the Commissioner, due under the terms of his or her appointment, must be paid out of the annual income of the States; and
-- src:806 | (7) Subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment under this paragraph must be met out of the annual income of the States.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7) (src:776) (src:806)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text`
      `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.9: the cost must be met out of the annual income of the States` interp `the vintage of the text` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` MEANS
    IF `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the vintage of the text`
    THEN CONSIDER interp's `a cost directed to the Fund`
         WHEN `the Fund bears the cost in place of the annual income of the States`
             THEN `F9.9 reading A: the Fund bears the cost the Order directs to it` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund`
         WHEN `the States remain liable and the Fund only reimburses`
             THEN `F9.9 reading B: the States remain liable and the Fund only reimburses` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund`
    ELSE TRUE

-- Reading A: where an Order directs the cost to the Fund, the annual income of the States is not what the cost must be met from. Reading B: it still is; the Fund only reimburses.
-- src:776 | (a) subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the remuneration or other payment for services of the Commissioner, due under the terms of his or her appointment, must be paid out of the annual income of the States; and
-- src:806 | (7) Subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment under this paragraph must be met out of the annual income of the States.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7) (src:776) (src:806)
GIVEN `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.9 reading A: the Fund bears the cost the Order directs to it` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` MEANS
    NOT `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7) (src:776) (src:806)
GIVEN `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.9 reading B: the States remain liable and the Fund only reimburses` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` MEANS
    TRUE

-- src:776 | (a) subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the remuneration or other payment for services of the Commissioner, due under the terms of his or her appointment, must be paid out of the annual income of the States; and
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(4)(a) (src:776)
@export Whether the remuneration of the Commissioner must be paid out of the annual income of the States in the chosen text of the Law, given whether an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which of the nine consolidated texts of the Law is read (decided by the temporal group)
      `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs a distribution from the Fund to the remuneration (an input: the Order is another enactment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 2(4)(a) the remuneration of the Commissioner must be paid out of the annual income of the States` interp `the vintage of the text` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` MEANS
    `F9.9: the cost must be met out of the annual income of the States` interp `the vintage of the text` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund`

-- 2(4)(b) names no payer; the person who receives the fees and sums is the Commissioner, so the Commissioner is read as the party who must pay them over (the actor is inferred, not stated).
-- The Law states no time for the payment, so the rule has no deadline. Not subject to the Dormant Bank Accounts Law.
-- src:777 | (b) all fees and other sums received by the Commissioner in the exercise of his or her functions must be paid to the income of the States.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 2(4)(b) (src:777)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 2(4)(b) all fees and other sums received by the Commissioner must be paid to the income of the States` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `Sch 1: the Commissioner pays fees and other sums to the income of the States`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "the fees and other sums received by the Commissioner were not paid to the income of the States"

§§ `3 Termination of office as Commissioner`

-- A notice of resignation under 3(1)(a). `the day the resignation takes effect` is the first day on which the person is no longer appointed, as the notice names it.
DECLARE `Notice of resignation of the Commissioner` HAS
    `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Commissioner gave the notice
    `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the notice was in writing and given to the Minister
    `the day the resignation takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person is no longer appointed, as the notice names it

-- The grounds of 3(2). The Minister's satisfaction on each ground is an input; the days of an absence are facts from which the Law's number (longer than 4 consecutive weeks) is computed.
-- F9.19: reading A, taken, requires both the Minister's satisfaction and an absence that really is longer than the number of weeks; reading B requires the Minister's satisfaction alone.
DECLARE `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner` HAS
    `the first day of absence from duties` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The first day of the absence of the person from his or her duties, if any
    `the last day of absence from duties` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The last day of that absence, if any
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (a): an input
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person has become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (b): an input
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person is incapacitated by illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (c): an input
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's satisfaction on ground (d): an input

-- A termination under 3(2).
DECLARE `Termination of the appointment of the Commissioner` HAS
    `the day the termination takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person is no longer appointed because the Minister terminated the appointment
    grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The grounds on which the Minister terminated

-- What may have ended the office of a person appointed as the Commissioner (3(1)(a) and (b)); expiry (3(1)(c)) is computed from the appointment.
DECLARE `Events that may end the office of the Commissioner` HAS
    resignation IS A MAYBE `Notice of resignation of the Commissioner` @desc The notice of resignation, if the person gave one
    termination IS A MAYBE `Termination of the appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The termination by the Minister, if there was one

-- 3(1) is the chapeau of the three cases below, which are combined in the rule `Sch 1 para 3(1) the person has ceased to be appointed as the Commissioner by the day` at the end of this paragraph.
-- src:779 | (1) A person ceases to be appointed as the Commissioner if –
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1) (src:779)
`Sch 1 para 3(1) a person ceases to be appointed as the Commissioner in these three cases (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(1) A person ceases to be appointed as the Commissioner if –"

-- src:780 | (a) he or she resigns from office by giving not less than 3 months’ notice in writing to the Minister;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1)(a) (src:780)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the notice of resignation must be for not less than this many months` MEANS 3

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1)(a) (src:780)
@export The first day on which a person is no longer appointed as the Commissioner because he or she resigned by giving not less than 3 months' notice in writing to the Minister, or NOTHING if the notice is not such a resignation
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      resignation IS A `Notice of resignation of the Commissioner` @desc The notice, the day it was given and the day it names as taking effect
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` interp resignation MEANS
    IF resignation's `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister`
    THEN `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` interp (resignation's `the day the notice was given`) (resignation's `the day the resignation takes effect`) `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the notice of resignation must be for not less than this many months`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1)(a) (src:780)
@export The Commissioner's power to resign by giving not less than 3 months' notice in writing to the Minister
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      resignation IS A `Notice of resignation of the Commissioner` @desc The notice of resignation: the day it was given, whether it was in writing to the Minister, and the day it names as taking effect
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the Commissioner may resign from office by giving not less than 3 months' notice in writing to the Minister` interp resignation MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MAY `Sch 1: the Commissioner resigns by notice in writing`
    PROVIDED isJust (`Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` interp resignation)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- 3(1)(b): the Minister terminates under 3(2), so the termination ends the office only if the Minister could terminate on the grounds (the gate is defined below, at 3(2)).
-- 3(1)(c): the appointment expires under 3(4) (defined below). Both are combined in the rule at the end of this paragraph.

-- 3(2) is a power of the Minister (encoded below as a MAY rule) whose chapeau is carried here and whose four grounds are encoded one by one.
-- src:783 | (2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a person as the Commissioner, after satisfying himself or herself that the person –
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2) (src:783)
`Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister may terminate the appointment after satisfying himself or herself on one of four grounds (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(2) The Minister may terminate the appointment of a person as the Commissioner, after satisfying himself or herself that the person –"

-- src:784 | (a) has been absent from his or her duties for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2)(a) (src:784)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the absence must be for a period longer than this many consecutive weeks` MEANS 4

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2)(a) (src:784)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` interp grounds MEANS
    CONSIDER grounds's `the first day of absence from duties`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST first
        THEN CONSIDER grounds's `the last day of absence from duties`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST last
                 THEN `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` interp first last `Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the absence must be for a period longer than this many consecutive weeks`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2)(a) (src:784)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` interp grounds MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: the ground of absence for terminating an appointment is made out` interp (grounds's `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks`) (`Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` interp grounds)

-- src:785 | (b) has become bankrupt;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2)(b) (src:785)
GIVEN grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(2)(b) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has become bankrupt` grounds MEANS
    grounds's `the Minister is satisfied that the person has become bankrupt`

-- src:786 | (c) is incapacitated by illness; or
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2)(c) (src:786)
GIVEN grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(2)(c) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is incapacitated by illness` grounds MEANS
    grounds's `the Minister is satisfied that the person is incapacitated by illness`

-- src:787 | (d) is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of the Commissioner.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2)(d) (src:787)
GIVEN grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(2)(d) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of the Commissioner` grounds MEANS
    grounds's `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of the Commissioner`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2) (src:783-787)
@export Whether the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on at least one of the four grounds on which he or she may terminate the appointment of the Commissioner
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The days of any absence and the Minister's satisfaction on each of the four grounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` interp grounds MEANS
        "(a)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has been absent for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` interp grounds
    OR  "(b)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(2)(b) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person has become bankrupt` grounds
    OR  "(c)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(2)(c) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is incapacitated by illness` grounds
    OR  "(d)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(2)(d) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of the Commissioner` grounds

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(2) (src:783-787)
@export The Minister's power to terminate the appointment of the Commissioner after satisfying himself or herself on one of four grounds
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      grounds IS A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The days of any absence and the Minister's satisfaction on each of the four grounds
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister may terminate the appointment of a person as the Commissioner` interp grounds MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Sch 1: the Minister terminates the appointment`
    PROVIDED `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` interp grounds
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- src:788 | (3) The Minister must, not more than 2 weeks after terminating the appointment, present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated the appointment.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(3) (src:788)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination must be presented not more than this many weeks after terminating` MEANS 2

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(3) (src:788)
@export The Minister's duty to present to the States, not more than 2 weeks after terminating the appointment of the Commissioner, a notice that he or she has terminated it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day of the termination` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister terminated the appointment
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 3(3) not more than 2 weeks after terminating the appointment the Minister must present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated it` interp `the day of the termination` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of the termination to the States`
    BEFORE (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of a termination` interp `the day of the termination` `Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination must be presented not more than this many weeks after terminating`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not present to the States a notice that the appointment was terminated not more than 2 weeks after terminating it"

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(3) (src:788)
@export Whether the notice that the Minister has terminated the appointment of the Commissioner was presented to the States in time, that is not more than 2 weeks after the termination, counted as the chosen reading says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day of the termination` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister terminated the appointment
      `the day on which the notice was presented to the States` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister presented the notice of the termination to the States
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` interp `the day of the termination` `the day on which the notice was presented to the States` MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` interp `the day of the termination` `the day on which the notice was presented to the States` `Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination must be presented not more than this many weeks after terminating`

-- 3(4) is the chapeau of the three cases below, which are combined in the rule `Sch 1 para 3(4) the day on which the appointment expires`.
-- src:789 | (4) A person’s appointment as the Commissioner expires if –
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4) (src:789)
`Sch 1 para 3(4) a person's appointment as the Commissioner expires in these three cases (chapeau, inert)` MEANS
    "(4) A person’s appointment as the Commissioner expires if –"

-- 3(4)(a): the period expires without re-appointment. If the term is followed by a re-appointment its end is not an expiry (the person goes on under the next appointment).
-- src:790 | (a) the period for which the person was appointed expires without re-appointment;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4)(a) (src:790)
GIVEN appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Sch 1 para 3(4)(a) the day the period of the appointment expires without re-appointment` appointment MEANS
    IF appointment's `the term is followed by a re-appointment`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (appointment's `the day the term expires`)

-- 3(4)(b): the person becomes a member of the States. F9.17: reading A, only becoming a member on or after the first day of the term ends the appointment;
-- reading B, being a member at any time during the appointment ends it, so a person already a member when appointed has the appointment expire on its first day.
-- src:791 | (b) the person becomes a member of the States; or
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4)(b) (src:791)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Sch 1 para 3(4)(b) the day the person becomes a member of the States` interp appointment MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which membership of the States ends the appointment` interp (appointment's `the day on which the person became a member of the States`) (appointment's `the first day of the term`)

-- src:792 | (c) the person completes 12 years (whether consecutive or in aggregate) of service as Commissioner.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4)(c) (src:792)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 1 para 3(4)(c) the day the person completes 12 years of service as the Commissioner` interp appointment MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` interp (appointment's `the service before this appointment`) (appointment's `the first day of the term`)

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4) (src:789-792)
@export The first day on which the appointment of the Commissioner has expired under paragraph 3(4): when the period of the appointment runs out without re-appointment, when the person becomes a member of the States, or when the person completes 12 years of service as Commissioner, whichever is first
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The appointment, the periods of service before it and any membership of the States
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 1 para 3(4) the day on which the appointment expires` interp appointment MEANS
    CONSIDER `Sch 1 and 2: the earlier of two optional days` (`Sch 1 para 3(4)(a) the day the period of the appointment expires without re-appointment` appointment) (`Sch 1 para 3(4)(b) the day the person becomes a member of the States` interp appointment)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Sch 1 para 3(4)(c) the day the person completes 12 years of service as the Commissioner` interp appointment
    WHEN JUST earlier THEN `Sch 1 and 2: the earlier of two days` earlier (`Sch 1 para 3(4)(c) the day the person completes 12 years of service as the Commissioner` interp appointment)

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(4) (src:789-792)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(4) the appointment has expired by the day` interp appointment `the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `Sch 1 para 3(4) the day on which the appointment expires` interp appointment

-- src:781 | (b) the Minister terminates his or her appointment under sub-paragraph (2); or
-- src:782 | (c) his or her appointment expires under sub-paragraph (4).
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1) (src:779-782)
@export Whether a person has ceased to be appointed as the Commissioner by the day in question: by resigning on not less than 3 months' notice in writing, by the Minister's termination under paragraph 3(2), or by expiry under paragraph 3(4)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      appointment IS AN `Appointment of the Commissioner` @desc The appointment in force and the facts that bear on its expiry
      events IS AN `Events that may end the office of the Commissioner` @desc Any notice of resignation and any termination by the Minister
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(1) the person has ceased to be appointed as the Commissioner by the day` interp appointment events `the day` MEANS
        "(a)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the person has resigned by the day` interp events `the day`
    OR  "(b)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(1)(b) the Minister has terminated the appointment by the day` interp events `the day`
    OR  "(c)" ... `Sch 1 para 3(4) the appointment has expired by the day` interp appointment `the day`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1)(a) (src:780)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      events IS AN `Events that may end the office of the Commissioner`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the person has resigned by the day` interp events `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER events's resignation
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST notice
        THEN CONSIDER `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` interp notice
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST ends THEN `the day` AT LEAST ends

-- src:781 | (b) the Minister terminates his or her appointment under sub-paragraph (2); or
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 3(1)(b) (src:781)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      events IS AN `Events that may end the office of the Commissioner`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 3(1)(b) the Minister has terminated the appointment by the day` interp events `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER events's termination
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST termination
        THEN     `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` interp (termination's grounds)
             AND `the day` AT LEAST termination's `the day the termination takes effect`

§§ `4 Staff, resources and reporting`

-- What the Minister has made available to the Commissioner (4(1)). The number of staff the Minister considers are required is the Minister's consideration: an input.
DECLARE `Staff made available to the Commissioner` HAS
    `the number of staff the Minister considers are required` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of staff the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the Commissioner's functions: an input
    `the number of staff made available` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of staff the Minister has made available to the Commissioner
    `the descriptions of staff made available are those the Minister considers are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the descriptions of staff made available match those the Minister considers are required: an input

-- src:794 | (1) The Minister must make available to the Commissioner such number and descriptions of staff as the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the Commissioner’s functions.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(1) (src:794)
GIVEN staff IS A `Staff made available to the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(1) the Minister has made available the number and descriptions of staff that the Minister considers are required` staff MEANS
        staff's `the number of staff made available` AT LEAST staff's `the number of staff the Minister considers are required`
    AND staff's `the descriptions of staff made available are those the Minister considers are required`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(1) (src:794)
@export The Minister's duty to make available to the Commissioner the number and descriptions of staff that the Minister considers are required
GIVEN staff IS A `Staff made available to the Commissioner` @desc What the Minister has made available: the number considered required, the number made available, and whether the descriptions match
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(1) the Minister must make available to the Commissioner such number and descriptions of staff as the Minister considers are required` staff MEANS
    IF `Sch 1 para 4(1) the Minister has made available the number and descriptions of staff that the Minister considers are required` staff
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 1: the Minister makes staff available`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not make available the number and descriptions of staff that the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the Commissioner's functions"

-- src:795 | (2) To the extent that any States’ employee (within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005), while made available under sub-paragraph (1), performs a function under the direction of the Commissioner, the employee is to be treated as a member of the Commissioner’s staff for the purposes of this Law.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(2) (src:795)
@export Whether a States' employee, made available to the Commissioner under paragraph 4(1), is treated as a member of the Commissioner's staff for a function the employee performs
GIVEN `the person is a States' employee within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the person is a States' employee (the status is defined by another Law: an input)
      `the employee was made available to the Commissioner under paragraph 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Minister made the employee available to the Commissioner under paragraph 4(1)
      `the employee performs the function under the direction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if, while made available, the employee performs the function under the direction of the Commissioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(2) the employee is to be treated as a member of the Commissioner's staff for the function` `the person is a States' employee within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005` `the employee was made available to the Commissioner under paragraph 4(1)` `the employee performs the function under the direction of the Commissioner` MEANS
        `the person is a States' employee within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005`
    AND `the employee was made available to the Commissioner under paragraph 4(1)`
    AND `the employee performs the function under the direction of the Commissioner`

-- 4(3): a function of the Commissioner may, to the extent authorized by the Commissioner, be exercised on the Commissioner's behalf by a member of staff, except three decisions.
-- The decision is `Decision of the Commissioner` (IP27): a subject (which Article) and an outcome. 4(3)(a) reserves the decision whether to register (either outcome) and 4(3)(c) the decision whether to deregister under Article 16 (either outcome).
-- 4(3)(b) reserves "the decision under Article 15(3) on whether to refuse to deregister": F9.8 reading A, taken, reserves that decision, either outcome (Article 15(3) is a single decision to deregister or to refuse);
-- reading B reserves only the refusal. F9.16: a decision on entry in the restricted section is made under Article 9(6) and (7), not Article 11: reading A, taken, does not reserve it; reading B reserves it as part of registering.
-- src:796 | (3) Any function of the Commissioner may, to the extent authorized by the Commissioner, be exercised on behalf of the Commissioner by any member of the Commissioner’s staff, except –
-- src:797 | (a) the decision under Article 11 on whether to register a charity;
-- src:798 | (b) the decision under Article 15(3) on whether to refuse to deregister a charity; and
-- src:799 | (c) the decision under Article 16 on whether to deregister a charity.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:796-799)
@export Whether the decision of the Commissioner is one that Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) reserves from members of the Commissioner's staff: the decision whether to register (Article 11), to refuse to deregister (Article 15(3)) or to deregister (Article 16)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the decision of the Commissioner` IS A `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The decision: which Article it is made under (its subject) and whether the Commissioner did what was sought or refused (its outcome)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` interp `the decision of the Commissioner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision of the Commissioner`'s subject
    WHEN `whether to register an applicant, Article 11` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`
        THEN CONSIDER interp's `the decision on entry in the restricted section`
             WHEN `it is not reserved because it is not a decision under Article 11` THEN `F9.16 reading A: the decision on entry in the restricted section is not reserved`
             WHEN `it is reserved as part of the decision whether to register` THEN `F9.16 reading B: the decision on entry in the restricted section is reserved`
    WHEN `whether to permit a change or addition of registered name, Article 12(4)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `whether to require a charity to apply to change its registered name, Article 12(6)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`
        THEN CONSIDER interp's `the decision under Article 15(3)`
             WHEN `both outcomes of the decision are reserved` THEN `F9.8 reading A: both outcomes of the decision under Article 15(3) are reserved` (`the decision of the Commissioner`'s outcome)
             WHEN `only the refusal is reserved` THEN `F9.8 reading B: only the refusal under Article 15(3) is reserved` (`the decision of the Commissioner`'s outcome)
    WHEN `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `whether to impose a requirement contained in a notice under Article 26` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other matter` THEN FALSE

-- Readings of the two forks in 4(3). F9.8, reading A (taken): the decision under Article 15(3) on whether to refuse to deregister is the single decision of 15(3), so either outcome is reserved.
-- Reading B: only the refusal is reserved, so staff may deregister an entity on its own application. F9.16, reading A (taken): the decision on entry in the restricted section is made under Article 9(6) and (7),
-- not Article 11, and is not reserved; reading B: it is part of the decision whether to register and is reserved.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(b) (src:798)
GIVEN outcome IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.8 reading A: both outcomes of the decision under Article 15(3) are reserved` outcome MEANS
    TRUE

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(b) (src:798)
GIVEN outcome IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.8 reading B: only the refusal under Article 15(3) is reserved` outcome MEANS
    outcome EQUALS `the Commissioner refuses`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(a) (src:797)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.16 reading A: the decision on entry in the restricted section is not reserved` MEANS
    FALSE

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(a) (src:797)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F9.16 reading B: the decision on entry in the restricted section is reserved` MEANS
    TRUE

-- src:797 | (a) the decision under Article 11 on whether to register a charity;
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(a) (src:797)
GIVEN `the decision of the Commissioner` IS A `Decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(3)(a) the decision is the decision under Article 11 on whether to register a charity` `the decision of the Commissioner` MEANS
    `the decision of the Commissioner`'s subject EQUALS `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`

-- src:798 | (b) the decision under Article 15(3) on whether to refuse to deregister a charity; and
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(b) (src:798)
GIVEN `the decision of the Commissioner` IS A `Decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(3)(b) the decision is the decision under Article 15(3) on whether to refuse to deregister a charity` `the decision of the Commissioner` MEANS
    `the decision of the Commissioner`'s subject EQUALS `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`

-- src:799 | (c) the decision under Article 16 on whether to deregister a charity.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)(c) (src:799)
GIVEN `the decision of the Commissioner` IS A `Decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(3)(c) the decision is the decision under Article 16 on whether to deregister a charity` `the decision of the Commissioner` MEANS
    `the decision of the Commissioner`'s subject EQUALS `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:796)
@export Whether a member of the Commissioner's staff may exercise a function on behalf of the Commissioner: the Commissioner has authorized it and it is not one of the decisions that paragraph 4(3) reserves
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the decision of the Commissioner` IS A `Decision of the Commissioner` @desc The function, as a decision: its subject and outcome (use the subject `any other matter` for a function that is not a decision)
      `the Commissioner has authorized the member of staff to exercise the function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE to the extent that the Commissioner has authorized the member of staff to exercise the function on the Commissioner's behalf
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(3) a member of the Commissioner's staff may exercise the function on behalf of the Commissioner` interp `the decision of the Commissioner` `the Commissioner has authorized the member of staff to exercise the function` MEANS
        `the Commissioner has authorized the member of staff to exercise the function`
    AND NOT `Sch 1 para 4(3) the decision is one that a member of the Commissioner's staff may not make on behalf of the Commissioner` interp `the decision of the Commissioner`

-- src:800 | (4) The Minister may designate a person as the relevant person for the purpose of sub-paragraph (5).
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(4) (src:800)
@export The Minister's power to designate a person as the relevant person who may be treated as the Commissioner
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(4) the Minister may designate a person as the relevant person for the purpose of sub-paragraph (5)` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Sch 1: the Minister designates a relevant person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- 4(5): a relevant person designated under 4(4) is treated as the Commissioner, temporarily, while (a) the appointee is unable to act through incapacity or absence, or (b) the office is vacant,
-- until the appointee is able to act again or a new Commissioner is appointed under paragraph 1. The Law sets no limit on how long that may last, and does not say whether a designation may be made before
-- the incapacity or vacancy begins: the rule asks only whether a designation is in place when (a) or (b) holds.
-- src:801 | (5) A relevant person designated under sub-paragraph (4) is to be treated as the Commissioner for the purposes of this Law, if –
-- src:802 | (a) the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence; or
-- src:803 | (b) there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner,
-- src:804 | on a temporary basis until the Commissioner becomes able to act again or a new Commissioner is appointed under paragraph 1.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5) (src:801-804)
GIVEN `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(5) the relevant person is treated as the Commissioner` `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` MEANS
        `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)`
    AND (    "(a)" ... `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence`
         OR  "(b)" ... `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner`)

-- src:802 | (a) the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence; or
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5)(a) (src:802)
GIVEN `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(5)(a) the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` MEANS
    `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence`

-- src:803 | (b) there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner,
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5)(b) (src:803)
GIVEN `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(5)(b) there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` MEANS
    `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner`

-- IP28: someone is acting as the Commissioner on the day in question if the person appointed is in office and able to act, or a designated relevant person is treated as the Commissioner.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(5) (src:801-804)
@export Whether someone is acting as the Commissioner: the person appointed is in office and able to act, or a relevant person designated by the Minister is treated as the Commissioner while the appointee is unable to act or the office is vacant
GIVEN `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Minister has designated a person as the relevant person under sub-paragraph (4)
      `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if a person is appointed as the Commissioner but is unable to act through incapacity or absence
      `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if no person is appointed as the Commissioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(5) someone is treated as the Commissioner` `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` MEANS
        (    NOT `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner`
         AND NOT `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence`)
    OR  `Sch 1 para 4(5) the relevant person is treated as the Commissioner` `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act through incapacity or absence` `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner`

-- src:805 | (6) The Minister must provide such accommodation and equipment as the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the Commissioner’s functions.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(6) (src:805)
@export The Minister's duty to provide the accommodation and equipment that the Minister considers are required for the Commissioner
GIVEN `the accommodation and equipment provided are those the Minister considers are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Minister has provided the accommodation and equipment that the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the Commissioner's functions: an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(6) the Minister must provide such accommodation and equipment as the Minister considers are required` `the accommodation and equipment provided are those the Minister considers are required` MEANS
    IF `the accommodation and equipment provided are those the Minister considers are required`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         MUST `Sch 1: the Minister provides accommodation and equipment`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not provide the accommodation and equipment that the Minister considers are required for the proper and effective discharge of the Commissioner's functions"

-- src:806 | (7) Subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment under this paragraph must be met out of the annual income of the States.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(7) (src:806)
@export Whether the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment to the Commissioner must be met out of the annual income of the States in the chosen text of the Law, given whether an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which of the nine consolidated texts of the Law is read (decided by the temporal group)
      `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs a distribution from the Fund to the cost (an input: the Order is another enactment)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(7) the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment must be met out of the annual income of the States` interp `the vintage of the text` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund` MEANS
    `F9.9: the cost must be met out of the annual income of the States` interp `the vintage of the text` `an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017 directs the cost to the Fund`

-- The report (4(8) to (10)). `the calendar year` is the year the report relates to. Publication is "publish" in the sense of Article 1: in a manner that, in the opinion of the person publishing, is likely to bring
-- the information to the attention of the public or of those affected: the Commissioner's opinion, an input. "As soon as practicable" is fork F9.10.
DECLARE `Report of the Commissioner on a calendar year` HAS
    `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the report relates to
    `the Commissioner has prepared the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Commissioner has prepared the report on the activities of the Commissioner in the year
    `the Commissioner has published the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Commissioner has published the report in a manner that, in the Commissioner's opinion, is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected (Article 1, "publish")
    `the day on which the report was provided to the Minister` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the Commissioner has not provided the report to the Minister
    `the report was provided as soon as practicable after the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that the Commissioner provided the report as soon as practicable (an input, used by the reading of F9.10 that takes it as a judgement)
    `the day on which the Minister laid a copy before the States` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the Minister has not laid a copy before the States
    `the copy was laid as soon as practicable after the Minister received the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that the Minister laid the copy as soon as practicable (an input, used by the reading of F9.10 that takes it as a judgement)

-- src:807 | (8) The Commissioner must prepare and publish a report on the activities of the Commissioner in each calendar year.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(8) (src:807)
@export The Commissioner's duty to prepare and publish a report on the activities of the Commissioner in a calendar year in which he or she held the office
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the first day on which the office was held` IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the person held the office (both ends of the holding are included)
      `the last day on which the office was held` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which the person held the office
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the report relates to
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(8) the Commissioner must prepare and publish a report on the activities of the Commissioner in each calendar year` interp `the first day on which the office was held` `the last day on which the office was held` `the calendar year` MEANS
    IF `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` interp `the first day on which the office was held` `the last day on which the office was held` `the calendar year`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `Sch 1: the Commissioner prepares and publishes the report`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "the Commissioner did not prepare and publish a report on the activities of the Commissioner in the calendar year"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(8) (src:807)
GIVEN report IS A `Report of the Commissioner on a calendar year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(8) the Commissioner has prepared and published the report` report MEANS
        report's `the Commissioner has prepared the report`
    AND report's `the Commissioner has published the report`

-- src:808 | (9) The Commissioner must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year to which the report relates, but in no case later than 4 months after the end of that year.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(9) (src:808)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 para 4(9) the report must be provided in no case later than this many months after the end of the year` MEANS 4

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(9) (src:808)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 1 para 4(9) the last day for providing the Minister with the report` interp `the calendar year` MEANS
    `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable and in no case after a day` interp (YMD `the calendar year` 12 31) (`Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a report on a calendar year` interp `the calendar year` `Sch 1 para 4(9) the report must be provided in no case later than this many months after the end of the year`)

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(9) (src:808)
@export The Commissioner's duty to provide the Minister with the report on a calendar year as soon as practicable after the year ends and in no case later than 4 months after it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the report relates to
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(9) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it` interp `the calendar year` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `Sch 1: the Commissioner provides the Minister with the report`
    BEFORE (`Sch 1 para 4(9) the last day for providing the Minister with the report` interp `the calendar year`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "the Commissioner did not provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it"

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(9) (src:808)
@export Whether the Commissioner provided the Minister with the report on a calendar year in time: as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it (30 April on the favoured reading)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      report IS A `Report of the Commissioner on a calendar year` @desc The report, the year it relates to and the day it was provided to the Minister
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(9) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the report in time` interp report MEANS
    CONSIDER report's `the day on which the report was provided to the Minister`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST provided
        THEN     `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` interp (report's `the calendar year`) provided `Sch 1 para 4(9) the report must be provided in no case later than this many months after the end of the year`
             AND `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` interp (report's `the report was provided as soon as practicable after the end of the year`) (YMD (report's `the calendar year`) 12 31) provided

-- src:809 | (10) The Minister must lay a copy of the report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after the Minister receives the report.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(10) (src:809)
@export The Minister's duty to lay a copy of the Commissioner's report before the States as soon as practicable after receiving it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      `the day on which the Minister received the report` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING if the Minister has not yet received the report
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(10) the Minister must lay a copy of the report so provided before the States as soon as practicable after receiving it` interp `the day on which the Minister received the report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the Minister received the report`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN JUST received
        THEN CONSIDER `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable` interp received
             WHEN NOTHING
                 THEN PARTY `the Minister`
                      MUST `Sch 1: the Minister lays a copy of the report before the States`
                      HENCE FULFILLED
                      LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not lay a copy of the report before the States as soon as practicable after receiving it"
             WHEN JUST last
                 THEN PARTY `the Minister`
                      MUST `Sch 1: the Minister lays a copy of the report before the States`
                      BEFORE last
                      HENCE FULFILLED
                      LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not lay a copy of the report before the States as soon as practicable after receiving it"

@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(10) (src:809)
@export Whether the Minister laid a copy of the report before the States as soon as practicable after receiving it
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings chosen for the counting of every period in Schedules 1 and 2 (the favoured reading of each fork is the default)
      report IS A `Report of the Commissioner on a calendar year` @desc The report and the days on which the Minister received it and laid a copy
      `the day on which the Minister received the report` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the Minister received the report from the Commissioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(10) the Minister laid a copy of the report before the States as soon as practicable` interp report `the day on which the Minister received the report` MEANS
    CONSIDER report's `the day on which the Minister laid a copy before the States`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST laid
        THEN `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` interp (report's `the copy was laid as soon as practicable after the Minister received the report`) `the day on which the Minister received the report` laid

-- src:810 | (11) The Minister may, by giving written notice to the Commissioner and publishing that notice, give directions to the Commissioner as to the content and form of the report.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(11) (src:810)
@export The Minister's power to give directions on the content and form of the Commissioner's report by written notice that is published
GIVEN `the notice is in writing and has been published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Minister's notice to the Commissioner is in writing and the Minister has published it
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(11) the Minister may, by giving written notice to the Commissioner and publishing that notice, give directions on the content and form of the report` `the notice is in writing and has been published` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `Sch 1: the Minister gives directions on the report`
    PROVIDED `the notice is in writing and has been published`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- 4(12) says "Directions under paragraph (11)"; the Schedule's paragraphs are numbered 1 to 4, so (11) is a sub-paragraph of paragraph 4: read as sub-paragraph (11).
-- src:811 | (12) Directions under paragraph (11) must respect the independence of the Commissioner and, in particular, must not require the report to contain justification of any decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(12) (src:811)
@export The prohibition on the Minister's directing that the Commissioner's report justify a decision about individual charities, governors or applicants
GIVEN `the direction requires the report to contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the direction requires the report to contain a justification of any decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Schedule 1`
`Sch 1 para 4(12) directions under sub-paragraph (11) must not require the report to contain justification of any decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration` `the direction requires the report to contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    SHANT `Sch 1: the Minister directs that the report justify a decision`
    PROVIDED `the direction requires the report to contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister directed that the report contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to an individual charity, governor or applicant for registration"

-- "must respect the independence of the Commissioner and, in particular, must not require ...": the general duty of respect is a judgement (an input); the particular limit is the prohibition above.
@ref Schedule 1 paragraph 4(12) (src:811)
@export Whether directions on the content and form of the report keep within paragraph 4(12): they respect the independence of the Commissioner and do not require the report to justify a decision of the Commissioner about individual charities, governors or applicants
GIVEN `the directions respect the independence of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that the directions respect the independence of the Commissioner: an input
      `the directions require the report to contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the directions require the report to contain a justification of any decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 4(12) the directions are within the limit` `the directions respect the independence of the Commissioner` `the directions require the report to contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration` MEANS
        `the directions respect the independence of the Commissioner`
    AND NOT `the directions require the report to contain justification of a decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration`
